        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "For $x=-2,-1,0,1,2$, respectively: $0.0540,\\ 0.2420,\\ 0.3989,\\ 0.2420,\\ 0.0540$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}f(-2)&=\\frac{e^{-2}}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}}\\approx0.0540\\\\f(0)&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}}\\approx0.3989\\\\f(2)&=\\frac{e^{-2}}{\\sqrt{2\\pi}}\\approx0.0540\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
      {
        "id": "p66-q1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Use the trapezoidal rule and 5 function values from part a to estimate $\\displaystyle\\int_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,dx$. Give your answer to 4 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$0.9369$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}h&=\\frac{2-(-2)}{5-1}=1\\\\\\int_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,dx&\\approx\\frac{1}{2}\\left[0.0540+2(0.2420+0.3989+0.2420)+0.0540\\right]\\\\\\int_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,dx&\\approx0.9369\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 21
      },
      {
        "id": "p66-q1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "The weights of Rhodesian ridgebacks are normally distributed with a mean of 48 kilograms and a standard deviation of 6 kilograms. Using the result from part b, calculate the probability of a randomly selected Rhodesian ridgeback weighing less than 36 kilograms. Give your answer as a percentage to 3 decimal places.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Approximately $0.03155$ ($3.155\\%$).",
          "worked": "Let $W$ be the weight in kilograms and $Z$ its standardised score.\n$$\\begin{aligned}z&=\\frac{36-48}{6}\\\\z&=-2\\end{aligned}$$\nBy symmetry, using the estimate from part b:\n$$\\begin{aligned}P(W<36)&=P(Z<-2)\\\\P(W<36)&\\approx\\frac{1-0.9369}{2}\\\\P(W<36)&\\approx0.03155=3.155\\%\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      }
    ]
